---
import Article from '../layouts/Article.astro';
---

<Article
  title="Privacy Policy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description="How Any Size collects, uses and protects personal information submitted through this website."
  lede="This policy covers information you give us through this website and how we use it."
  crumbs={[]}
>
  <div class="admin-note">
    <strong>Publish note — remove before launch.</strong> This is a starting template, not
    legal advice. Have it reviewed against the privacy laws that apply to you before going
    live — that may include state laws such as the CCPA, Canadian PIPEDA if you sell into
    Canada, and GDPR if you accept enquiries from the EU. Fill in your business name, contact
    address and any analytics or advertising tools you actually use.
  </div>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>We collect information you submit directly through our quote and contact forms:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Name, email address and phone number</li>
    <li>Delivery ZIP or postal code, and site address where you provide it</li>
    <li>Details about the building you are enquiring about</li>
    <li>Anything else you choose to include in a message</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Our web host also records standard technical information such as IP address, browser type
    and pages visited, as part of operating the site.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To prepare and send you a quote</li>
    <li>To follow up about your enquiry</li>
    <li>To arrange engineering, production and delivery if you place an order</li>
    <li>To meet legal and record-keeping obligations</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not sell your personal information. We share it only with the parties needed to
    fulfil your enquiry or order — for example our manufacturing partner, the engineer
    preparing your stamped drawings, and the freight carrier delivering your kit.
  </p>

  <h2>Marketing</h2>
  <p>
    If we send you occasional updates, every message includes a way to unsubscribe, and we
    will stop when you ask. You can also ask us to stop at any time using the contact details
    on this site.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention</h2>
  <p>
    We keep enquiry records while your enquiry is active and for a reasonable period
    afterwards. Order records are retained longer, because warranty and engineering
    documentation needs to remain available for the life of the building.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have the right to request a copy of the information
    we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it. Contact us using the
    details on this site and we will respond.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This site uses cookies only where needed to operate properly. If we add analytics or
    advertising tools later, this section will be updated to say what they are and what they
    collect.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy can be sent to us through the
    <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</Article>

<style>
  .admin-note {
    padding: 1rem 1.125rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, #dc2626 8%, transparent);
    border: 1px dashed color-mix(in srgb, #dc2626 45%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--radius); font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .admin-note strong { display: block; color: #dc2626; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
</style>
